  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.4. Increased capacity of ILO constituents to strengthen legislation, polices and measures to ensure equal opportunities and treatment in the world of work for persons with disabilities and other persons in vulnerable situations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of Liberia adopted a work place policy on HIV/AIDS in August 2021.  

The Policy was informed by the information gathered by the Ministry of Labour and the National AIDS Commission in collaboration with the Ministry of Education during the celebration of a Training of Trainers on HIV/AIDS awareness in the workplace on March 18 &#x2013; 19, 2021 for 40 School Teachers in Rural Montserrado. The ILO supported financially and facilitated the development of the National HIV and AIDS Workplace Policy and supported the hosting of a number of meetings by the Technical Working Group on the revision and validation of this Policy.  

On March 18 &#x2013; 19, 2021 the ILO supported the the Ministry of Labour and the National AIDS Commission and the Ministry of Education and facilitated a Training of Trainers Workshop on HIV/AIDS awareness for 40 public School teachers and staff from the Ministries of Labour and Education in Rural Montserradoa.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">6.4.1. Number of member States that have measures to ensure equality of opportunities and treatment for persons with disabilities and for at least one of the following groups: indigenous or tribal peoples; ethnic minorities; persons living with HIV; or LGBTI persons</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
